# Canonicalize author identities for `git shortlog`, `git log`, and AUTHORS
# generation.
#
# Every canonical name below appears verbatim in existing history. Where a
# contributor used several forms, the entry picks the fullest one they actually
# wrote; no name is inferred from a username, email local-part, or GitHub login.
#
# Note: GitHub's contributor graph does NOT read this file. It links commits to
# accounts by the commit author email. To consolidate a split graph, add every
# address below to the corresponding GitHub account's verified email list.
#
# Deliberately NOT merged, because the evidence is ambiguous:
#   - `kursathalat` <86690946+kursathalat@...> and `Kürşat Aktaş`
#     <kursat.ce@gmail.com> may be one person, but the surnames differ.
#   - `Leire Aguirre Eguiluz` and `Leire Rosado` <34123971+leireropl@...> are
#     treated as different people; the surnames differ.
#   - `José Francisco Calvo` is not `Francisco Aranda`.
#   - 42 commits authored as `you <you@example.com>` cannot be attributed.

